{"name":"Queen Anne’s Lace","hex":"#f2eede","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"queen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The wife, consort, or widow of a king.","A female monarch."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To act the part of a queen; to behave imperiously; to queen it.","To make a queen or (figuratively) to give the status of a queen."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/queen"},{"term":"lace","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A light fabric containing patterns of holes, usually built up from a single thread.","A cord or ribbon passed through eyelets in a shoe or garment, pulled tight and tied to fasten the shoe or garment firmly."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fasten (something) with laces.","To interweave items."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lace"}],"entries":[{"title":"Queen Anne's lace","blocks":[{"text":"Queen Anne's lace is a common name for a number of plants in the family Apiaceae,\nincluding:"},{"items":["Ammi majus, native to the Nile River Valley","Anthriscus sylvestris, a herbaceous biennial or short-lived perennial plant","Daucus carota, native to temperate Eurasia and naturalized in Australia and North America; the wild form of the domesticated carrot"]}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/DaucusCarota.jpg/330px-DaucusCarota.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Queen_Anne's_lace"},{"title":"Lace","blocks":[{"text":"Lace is a decorative openwork textile made without the use of pre-existing fabric. Lace can be made by hand or machine. Various techniques can be employed to form lace, each having a distinct category. Lace can also be used to refer to other types of openwork fabric such as cutwork or filet, which use pre-existing fabric."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Verknipte_kantstrook.JPG/330px-Verknipte_kantstrook.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lace"},{"title":"Anne","blocks":[{"text":"Anne, alternatively spelled Ann, is a form of the Latin female name Anna. This in turn is a representation of the Hebrew Hannah, which means 'favour' or 'grace'. Related names include Annie and Ana."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Dahl%2C_Michael_-_Queen_Anne_-_NPG_6187.jpg/330px-Dahl%2C_Michael_-_Queen_Anne_-_NPG_6187.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anne"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Ammi_majus_002.JPG/120px-Ammi_majus_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Ammi_majus_002.JPG/250px-Ammi_majus_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Ammi_majus_002.JPG/120px-Ammi_majus_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAmmi_majus_002.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Anthriscus_sylvestris003.jpg/120px-Anthriscus_sylvestris003.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Anthriscus_sylvestris003.jpg/250px-Anthriscus_sylvestris003.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Anthriscus_sylvestris003.jpg/120px-Anthriscus_sylvestris003.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnthriscus_sylvestris003.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/